 {
  "name": "reserve brings only the JD spelling of a term the page says another way",
  "why": "JD has 'alphas' twice, so the cluster's jd_spelling is 'alphas'; the page holds 'alpha'. The reserve thus brings 'the terms it holds in the jd_spelling while the page holds them only in another spelling'. The swap rule does not apply because singular/plural is explicitly not a bullet variant ('workflow'/'workflows' is NOT allowed). Removing the second bullet loses no term because 'alpha' remains in the third; removing the third would lose 'delta', so the second is replaced. Order then puts 'alpha delta' (2 terms) before 'alphas' (1 term).",
